TEXT 64 -272 Left 2 ;8-bit SAR ADC with charge redistribution. One conversion takes 10 clock cycles, in three phases that never overlap:\n1) Sample (smp = 1): Stop puts the top plate on vcm and Ssmp the bottom plates of the binary array (C7 = 128 Cu … C0 = Cu) on vin.\n2) Hold (every switch open): the floating top plate keeps that charge, which is the sample.\n3) Eight trials: Sref and Sgnd put each bottom plate on vref (up[k], the bits at 1 of the code being tried) or on ground (dn[k]): then top = vcm − vin·255/256 + vref·code/256.\nThe comparator (COMP, a CMOS subcircuit of the project) says whether top is below vcm, that is, whether vin is above the trial voltage,\nand SARLOGIC.v keeps or drops each bit, MSB first. Result: data = vin·255/vref, once every 10 clock cycles (100 kS/s at 1 MHz).\nThe switches (ASW) are a «Model» module of the project: the XSPICE analog switch, which changes its resistance smoothly.
TEXT 1136 672 Left 2 ;R-2R DAC, only to see data as a voltage:\ndac = 5 V · data / 256
TEXT 64 928 Left 2 !.param Cu=100f
TEXT 64 960 Left 2 !.tran 2m
